alwaysApply: true
---

@rule acceptance_checklist
Before finalizing code changes, verify all applicable items:

## Entity
- [ ] Extends `BaseEntityCustom` with explicit `@Entity('table_name')` or `@Entity({ name: 'table_name' })`.
- [ ] Table name is plural snake_case (e.g., `articles`, `comments`).
- [ ] Properties/columns use camelCase (e.g., `userId`, `createdAt`).
- [ ] JoinColumn uses camelCase names (`@JoinColumn({ name: 'userId' })`).
- [ ] JoinTable (M2M) uses snake_case for table and columns (`article_tags`, `article_id`).
- [ ] Proper indexes defined for frequently queried fields.
- [ ] Foreign key columns have corresponding relation decorators.

## Service
- [ ] Extends `BaseService<T>` with proper configuration.
- [ ] Cache prefix configured (unique per entity).
- [ ] `relationsWhitelist` configured for security.
- [ ] `selectWhitelist` configured to prevent sensitive field exposure.
- [ ] `getSearchableColumns()` returns appropriate fields.
- [ ] Lifecycle hooks used for side effects (cache invalidation, notifications).
- [ ] Complex operations use `runInTransaction()`.
- [ ] Logger instantiated: `private readonly logger = new Logger(ClassName.name)`.

## Controller
- [ ] Thin—no business logic; all logic in services.
- [ ] `@Auth()` decorator on protected endpoints.
- [ ] `@TrackEvent()` decorator on CRUD endpoints.
- [ ] `@UseInterceptors(AnalyticsInterceptor)` applied (class or method level).
- [ ] `SnowflakeIdPipe` used for ID parameters.
- [ ] `@RequirePermissions()` used where fine-grained access is needed.

## Module
- [ ] `TypeOrmModule.forFeature([Entity])` imported.
- [ ] `AnalyticsModule` imported (for `@TrackEvent` support).
- [ ] `PermissionsModule` imported (for `@RequirePermissions` support).
- [ ] Service exported if needed by other modules.

## DTOs & Validation
- [ ] All DTOs use `class-validator` decorators.
- [ ] Pagination `limit` clamped to 1..100.
- [ ] Proper `@Transform()` decorators for type conversion.

## Pagination
- [ ] `listCursor()` uses signed cursors (`encodeSignedCursor`/`decodeSignedCursor`).
- [ ] Custom cursor methods document exceptions if using unsigned cursors.
- [ ] Response format matches contract (offset or cursor metadata).

## Query Building
- [ ] `ConditionBuilder` used for dynamic filters.
- [ ] No raw SQL string concatenation.
- [ ] Search fields validated against `getSearchableColumns()`.

## Caching
- [ ] Cache keys use proper prefix format (`${prefix}:id:${id}`, `${prefix}:list:${hash}`).
- [ ] Cache invalidation in `afterCreate`/`afterUpdate`/`afterDelete` hooks.
- [ ] SWR enabled where appropriate (`swrSec > 0`).

## Error Handling
- [ ] Errors use i18n message keys (`{ messageKey: 'domain.ERROR_KEY' }`).
- [ ] No internal details leaked in error responses.
- [ ] Proper HTTP status codes used.

## Async Processing
- [ ] Heavy async processing uses RabbitMQ.
- [ ] Simple domain events MAY use EventEmitter (document choice).

## General
- [ ] No migrations or generators used.
- [ ] All package commands use Yarn.
- [ ] Comments in English, clear and detailed.
- [ ] No hardcoded secrets or sensitive data.
